>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p class="lede">Something not working, or an idea for the app? Email <a href="mailto:pindropapp@proton.me?subject=Pindrop%20Support">pindropapp@proton.me</a> and I'll get back to you.</p>
  <p>It helps to mention your iPhone model and iOS version. You can also write from the app: Contact Me in Settings adds the app version for you.</p>

  <h2>How do I score a throw?</h2>
  <p>Pull a player's tag down. The further you drag, the more points (up to 12). Drag it up to log a miss.</p>

  <h2>How many players can play?</h2>
  <p>2–8 players or teams. Tap the people button at the bottom left to add, remove or rename them.</p>

  <h2>I scored the wrong player</h2>
  <p>Tap undo to take back the last move. Hold it to see every step of the game and go back to any point.</p>

  <h2>What rules does Pindrop follow?</h2>
  <p>First to exactly 50 wins. Go over 50 and you drop back to 25. Three misses in a row and you're out. The full rules are under How to Play in Settings.</p>

  <h2>The screen keeps turning off</h2>
  <p>Turn on Keep Screen On in Settings, and the screen stays awake while you play.</p>

  <h2>Will I lose my game if I close the app?</h2>
  <p>No. Your game waits for you next time you open Pindrop.</p>
</AppPage>
